A1. This is often seen on a German student's face. ~ SCAR
A5. If you've spoken out of turn you've done this. ~ SAID
A9. Sir Thomas Lipton would not enter this kind of boat in a race. ~ SCOW
A13. A mushy highway. ~ LANE
A14. A whole lot. ~ ACRE
A15. Do this with a hard problem. ~ COPE
A16. Picnic accessories. ~ ANTS
A17. To make a touch. ~ FEEL
A18. Salutations. ~ AVES
A19. Sacred insects. ~ BEETLES
A21. What the infant prodigy sometimes lacks. ~ TALENT
A23. Something to put a ring on. ~ EAR
A24. This often goes out into the sea. ~ CAPE
A25. Baby nails. ~ BRADS
A28. Often this means "yes." ~ NO
A29. What the ball-player often gets credit for. ~ ERROR
A33. Detroit is putting a crimp in this cereal. ~ OAT
A34. The most lasting part of a bunch of flowers. ~ STEMS
A37. More than none. ~ SOME
A38. The first thing you do when you run into a stone wall. ~ STOP
A40. An ordinary Mexican. ~ REBEL
A42. You can get fried on this. ~ PAN
A43. The leaf of the calyx. ~ SEPAL
A45. Part of the D. S. C. ~ DS
A46. To prevent. ~ AVERT
A48. These wear the fighter down. ~ JABS
A50. The usual Christmas present. ~ TIE
A51. To scrape. ~ ABRADE
A54. This is right in order. ~ ORDINAL
A58. You'll never find this at the ringside. ~ ROOM
A59. Hot inside stuff. ~ LAVA
A61. Unmarried. ~ LONE
A62. Where Napoleon thought it over. ~ ELBA
A63. What the modern girl ought to be. ~ CLAD
A64. This pours it out good and hot. ~ ETNA
A65. These cause foam at the mug. ~ ALES
A66. Hearty's running-mate. ~ HALE
A67. What you will be after you die. ~ DEAD

D1. This will be over your head. ~ SLAB
D2. One of Chaplin's props. ~ CANE
D3. A kitty. ~ ANTE
D4. How the night watchman feels the morning after. ~ RESTED
D5. The way you feel out of Chicago. ~ SAFER
D6. Parts of a deck. ~ ACES
D7. You shouldn't get this up in the morning. ~ IRE
D8. This is in some mouths. ~ DELTA
D9. Fish undressers. ~ SCALERS
D10. Small harbor. ~ COVE
D11. The way your mind should be. ~ OPEN
D12. The home of the butter-and-egger. ~ WEST
D20. Who the lad loves. ~ LASS
D22. Darwin's relative. ~ APE
D24. What the modern girl does to her hair. ~ COMBS
D25. The man who doesn't have to punch the clock. ~ BOSS
D26. What Bradstreet does. ~ RATE
D27. Where the flagpole-sitter can be found. ~ ATOP
D28. States requiring relief. ~ NEEDS
D30. The electric chair is substituting for this. ~ ROPE
D31. The big bread-and-wine boy from the East. ~ OMAR
D32. A good opening for a seamstress. ~ RENT
D35. A president's initials. ~ TR
D36. Compass point. ~ SE
D39. Evening clothes for the tired business man. ~ PAJAMAS
D41. What the setting hen did. ~ LAID
D44. A youth. ~ LAD
D47. The Turkish woman did this to her face after it was lifted. ~ VEILED
D49. To eject with violence. ~ BELCH
D50. The Smith Brother on the left. ~ TRADE
D51. The lack of this causes skyscrapers. ~ AREA
D52. The queen of diamonds. ~ BOLL
D53. A garment for a night of the bath. ~ ROBE
D54. The kind of shape the football is in after a tough game. ~ OVAL
